1. Ignite about 6 quarts (1 large chimney or about 6 pounds) of charcoal and burn until coals are completely covered with a thin coating of light gray ash, 20 to 30 minutes. Spread coals evenly over grill bottom, position grill rack above the coals, and heat until medium-hot (you can hold your hand 5 inches above grill surface for no longer than 3 or 4 seconds).

